  #|upstream complete
  #|case llhttp request/lenient-headers.md:6
  #|name Header value (lenient)
  #|side request
  #|wire GET /url HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: h\r\nHeader1: \x0c\r\n\r\n
  #|note Host: h added after the request line
  #|note llhttp mode request-lenient-headers
  #|reason llhttp's lenient mode accepts a control character in a field value; mttp refuses it (CONTRACT.md "HTTP/1 codec": controls are refused; RFC 9110 section 5.5 field-vchar excludes CTL).
  #|expect refused Malformed
  #|upstream request GET /url 1.1
  #|upstream header host: h
  #|upstream header header1: \x0c
  #|upstream complete
  #|case llhttp request/lenient-headers.md:34
  #|name Second request header value (lenient)
  #|side request
  #|wire GET /url HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: h\r\nHeader1: Okay\r\n\r\n\r\nGET /url HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: h\r\nHeader1: \x0c\r\n\r\n
  #|note Host: h added after the request line
  #|note llhttp mode request-lenient-headers
  #|reason llhttp's lenient mode accepts a control character in a field value; mttp refuses it (CONTRACT.md "HTTP/1 codec": controls are refused; RFC 9110 section 5.5 field-vchar excludes CTL).
  #|expect request GET /url 1.1
  #|expect header host: h
  #|expect header header1: Okay
  #|expect complete
  #|expect refused Malformed
  #|upstream request GET /url 1.1
  #|upstream header host: h
  #|upstream header header1: Okay
  #|upstream complete
  #|upstream request GET /url 1.1
  #|upstream header host: h
  #|upstream header header1: \x0c
  #|upstream complete
  #|case llhttp request/lenient-headers.md:109
  #|name Empty headers separated by CR (lenient)
  #|side request
  #|wire POST / HTTP/1.1\r\nConnection: Close\r\nHost: localhost:5000\r\nx:\rTransfer-Encoding: chunked\r\n\r\n1\r\nA\r\n0\r\n
  #|note llhttp mode request-lenient-headers
  #|reason llhttp's lenient mode accepts a bare CR or LF as a line end; mttp requires CRLF (CONTRACT.md "HTTP/1 codec": strict CRLF; h1 README "What is refused": bare CR or LF).
  #|expect refused Malformed
  #|upstream request POST / 1.1
  #|upstream header connection: Close
  #|upstream header host: localhost:5000
  #|upstream header x: 
  #|upstream header transfer-encoding: chunked
  #|upstream body A
  #|upstream incomplete
  #|case llhttp request/lenient-header-value-relaxed.md:8
  #|name Control char in header value (relaxed)
  #|side request
  #|wire GET /url HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: h\r\nHeader1: hello\x0cworld\r\n\r\n
  #|note Host: h added after the request line
  #|note llhttp mode request-lenient-header-value-relaxed
  #|reason llhttp's lenient mode accepts a control character in a field value; mttp refuses it (CONTRACT.md "HTTP/1 codec": controls are refused; RFC 9110 section 5.5 field-vchar excludes CTL).
  #|expect refused Malformed
  #|upstream request GET /url 1.1
  #|upstream header host: h
  #|upstream header header1: hello\x0cworld
  #|upstream complete
  #|case llhttp request/lenient-header-value-relaxed.md:38
  #|name Consecutive control chars return to the ordinary header scanner
  #|side request
  #|wire GET /url HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: h\r\nHeader1: hello\x0c\x0cworld\r\n\r\n
  #|note Host: h added after the request line
  #|note llhttp mode request-lenient-header-value-relaxed
  #|reason llhttp's lenient mode accepts a control character in a field value; mttp refuses it (CONTRACT.md "HTTP/1 codec": controls are refused; RFC 9110 section 5.5 field-vchar excludes CTL).
  #|expect refused Malformed
  #|upstream request GET /url 1.1
  #|upstream header host: h
  #|upstream header header1: hello\x0c\x0cworld
  #|upstream complete
  #|case llhttp request/lenient-header-value-relaxed.md:190
  #|name Space after start line must still fail
  #|side request
  #|wire GET /url HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: h\r\n Header1: value\r\n
  #|note Host: h added after the request line
  #|note llhttp mode request-lenient-header-value-relaxed
  #|reason The input ends before the empty line that ends the head. llhttp refuses at the offending byte; mttp parses a head once it is complete, so it waits for more bytes, and its engines refuse the truncated head at the end of input.
  #|expect incomplete
  #|upstream refused Malformed
  #|case llhttp request/lenient-version.md:4
  #|name Invalid HTTP version (lenient)
  #|side request
  #|wire GET / HTTP/5.6\r\n\r\n
  #|note llhttp mode request-lenient-version
  #|reason llhttp's lenient mode accepts an HTTP version other than 1.x; mttp refuses it as unsupported (h1 README "What is refused": an HTTP version other than 1.x; h1server README "Strict framing": 505).
  #|expect refused Unsupported
  #|upstream request GET / 5.6
  #|upstream complete
  #|case llhttp request/method.md:96
  #|name CONNECT with body
  #|side request
  #|wire CONNECT foo.bar.com:443 HTTP/1.0\r\nUser-agent: Mozilla/1.1N\r\nProxy-authorization: basic aGVsbG86d29ybGQ=\r\nContent-Length: 10\r\n\r\nblarfcicle"
  #|reason mttp's codec frames a CONNECT request by its Content-Length like any other request; llhttp hands the bytes after the head to the tunnel. RFC 9110 section 9.3.6 gives CONNECT no content, and mttp's server answers CONNECT with 501 and closes (h1server README "Strict framing"), so the body is never tunnelled.
  #|expect request CONNECT foo.bar.com:443 1.0
  #|expect header user-agent: Mozilla/1.1N
  #|expect header proxy-authorization: basic aGVsbG86d29ybGQ=
  #|expect header content-length: 10
  #|expect body blarfcicle
  #|expect complete
  #|expect handoff
  #|upstream request CONNECT foo.bar.com:443 1.0
  #|upstream header user-agent: Mozilla/1.1N
  #|upstream header proxy-authorization: basic aGVsbG86d29ybGQ=
  #|upstream header content-length: 10
  #|upstream complete
  #|upstream handoff
  #|case llhttp request/method.md:135
  #|name M-SEARCH request
  #|side request
  #|wire M-SEARCH * HTTP/1.1\r\nHOST: 239.255.255.250:1900\r\nMAN: "ssdp:discover"\r\nST: "ssdp:all"\r\n\r\n
  #|reason The asterisk-form target is only for OPTIONS (RFC 9112 section 3.2.4), so SSDP's `M-SEARCH *` is refused.
  #|expect refused Malformed
  #|upstream request M-SEARCH * 1.1
  #|upstream header host: 239.255.255.250:1900
  #|upstream header man: "ssdp:discover"
  #|upstream header st: "ssdp:all"
  #|upstream complete
  #|case llhttp request/uri.md:4
  #|name Quotes in URI
  #|side request
  #|wire GET /with_"lovely"_quotes?foo=\\"bar\\" HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: h\r\n\r\n
  #|note Host: h added after the request line
  #|reason A request target with characters outside RFC 3986 (here `"` and `\`) is refused (RFC 9112 section 3.2; h1 README "What is refused": an invalid target form).
  #|expect refused Malformed
  #|upstream request GET /with_"lovely"_quotes?foo=\\"bar\\" 1.1
  #|upstream header host: h
  #|upstream complete
  #|case llhttp request/uri.md:165
  #|name Fragment in URI
  #|side request
  #|wire GET /forums/1/topics/2375?page=1#posts-17408 HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: h\r\n\r\n
  #|note Host: h added after the request line
  #|reason A request target with a fragment is refused: origin-form has none (RFC 9112 section 3.2.1; h1 README "What is refused": an invalid target form). These cases' targets carry `#hey`, so the fragment is refused before the transfer coding the case is about, which is refused too where it is not a single chunked.
  #|expect refused Malformed
  #|upstream request GET /forums/1/topics/2375?page=1#posts-17408 1.1
  #|upstream header host: h
  #|upstream complete
  #|case llhttp request/uri.md:222
  #|name `host:port` and basic auth
  #|side request
  #|wire GET http://a%12:b!&*$@hypnotoad.org:1234/toto HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: h\r\n\r\n
  #|note Host: h added after the request line
  #|reason An absolute-form target with userinfo is refused: RFC 9110 section 4.2.4 deprecates userinfo in http URIs and has recipients treat it as an error.
  #|expect refused Malformed
  #|upstream request GET http://a%12:b!&*$@hypnotoad.org:1234/toto 1.1
  #|upstream header host: h
  #|upstream complete
  #|case llhttp request/connection.md:107
  #|name Resetting flags when keep-alive is off (1.0, lenient)
  #|side request
  #|wire PUT /url HTTP/1.0\r\nContent-Length: 0\r\n\r\nPUT /url HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: h\r\nTransfer-Encoding: chunked\r\n\r\n
  #|note Host: h added after the request line
  #|note llhttp mode request-lenient-keep-alive
  #|reason llhttp's lenient mode reads on after a message that ends the connection; mttp's engines close it there (h1server README "Peers": HTTP/1.0 keeps a connection only when it asks for keep-alive; Connection: close ends it, RFC 9112 section 9.6).
  #|expect request PUT /url 1.0
  #|expect header content-length: 0
  #|expect complete
  #|expect closed
  #|upstream request PUT /url 1.0
  #|upstream header content-length: 0
  #|upstream complete
  #|upstream request PUT /url 1.1
  #|upstream header host: h
  #|upstream header transfer-encoding: chunked
  #|upstream incomplete
  #|case llhttp request/connection.md:392
  #|name CRLF between requests, explicit `close` (lenient)
  #|side request
  #|wire POST / HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: www.example.com\r\nContent-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded\r\nContent-Length: 4\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\nq=42\r\n\r\nGET / HTTP/1.1
  #|note llhttp mode request-lenient-keep-alive
  #|reason llhttp's lenient mode reads on after a message that ends the connection; mttp's engines close it there (h1server README "Peers": HTTP/1.0 keeps a connection only when it asks for keep-alive; Connection: close ends it, RFC 9112 section 9.6).
  #|expect request POST / 1.1
  #|expect header host: www.example.com
  #|expect header content-type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
  #|expect header content-length: 4
  #|expect header connection: close
  #|expect body q=42
  #|expect complete
  #|expect closed
  #|upstream request POST / 1.1
  #|upstream header host: www.example.com
  #|upstream header content-type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
  #|upstream header content-length: 4
  #|upstream header connection: close
  #|upstream body q=42
  #|upstream complete
  #|upstream incomplete
  #|case llhttp request/connection.md:481
  #|name Multiple tokens with folding
