  #|case llhttp request/content-length.md:75
  #|name Error on `Content-Length` overflow
  #|side request
  #|wire PUT /url HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: h\r\nContent-Length: 1000000000000000000000\r\n
  #|note Host: h added after the request line
  #|reason The input ends before the empty line that ends the head. llhttp refuses at the offending byte; mttp parses a head once it is complete, so it waits for more bytes, and its engines refuse the truncated head at the end of input.
  #|expect incomplete
  #|upstream refused Malformed
  #|case llhttp request/content-length.md:100
  #|name Error on duplicate `Content-Length`
  #|side request
  #|wire PUT /url HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: h\r\nContent-Length: 1\r\nContent-Length: 2\r\n
  #|note Host: h added after the request line
  #|reason The input ends before the empty line that ends the head. llhttp refuses at the offending byte; mttp parses a head once it is complete, so it waits for more bytes, and its engines refuse the truncated head at the end of input.
  #|expect incomplete
  #|upstream refused Malformed
  #|case llhttp request/content-length.md:189
  #|name Invalid whitespace token with `Content-Length` header field (lenient)
  #|side request
  #|wire PUT /url HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: h\r\nConnection: upgrade\r\nContent-Length : 4\r\nUpgrade: ws\r\n\r\nabcdefgh
  #|note Host: h added after the request line
  #|note llhttp mode request-lenient-headers
  #|reason llhttp's lenient mode accepts whitespace between a field name and its colon; mttp refuses it, as RFC 9112 section 5.1 requires of a server (CONTRACT.md "HTTP/1 codec").
  #|expect refused Malformed
  #|upstream request PUT /url 1.1
  #|upstream header host: h
  #|upstream header connection: upgrade
  #|upstream header content-length : 4
  #|upstream header upgrade: ws
  #|upstream body abcd
  #|upstream complete
  #|upstream handoff
  #|case llhttp request/content-length.md:229
  #|name No error on simultaneous `Content-Length` and `Transfer-Encoding: identity` (lenient)
  #|side request
  #|wire PUT /url HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: h\r\nContent-Length: 1\r\nTransfer-Encoding: identity\r\n\r\n
  #|note Host: h added after the request line
  #|note llhttp mode request-lenient-chunked-length
  #|reason llhttp's lenient mode accepts Content-Length with Transfer-Encoding; mttp refuses it as smuggling (CONTRACT.md "HTTP/1 codec": CL+TE is rejected as smuggling; h1server README "Strict framing").
  #|expect refused Smuggling
  #|upstream request PUT /url 1.1
  #|upstream header host: h
  #|upstream header content-length: 1
  #|upstream header transfer-encoding: identity
  #|upstream incomplete
  #|case llhttp request/content-length.md:519
  #|name Missing CRLF-CRLF before body (lenient)
